# diagnostic-mode: compile
# expect-code: E2S154
# expect-span: byte 447
# Every malformed `par` used to report the same sentence at the `par` token, so
# a missing block, a missing scope name and a missing bar were one message at
# one byte — the diagnostic said the construct was unimplemented rather than
# that it was mistyped. The shape is checked first now, and the byte named is
# the token that does not fit.
fn main() {
    par |scope|
}
